  "explanation": {
    "markdown": "## Can, can’t: Grammar chart\n\n![Grammar chart displaying the form and use of modal verbs 'can' and 'can't' for expressing ability, permission, and possibility, with correct and incorrect example sentences.](/uploads/grammar/a1/can-cant/img-1.jpg)\n\n## Can, can’t: Form\n\n#### Infinitive without **to**\n\nWe use **can** + **[infinitive](https://test-english.com/grammar-points/a1/verbs-infinitive-verbs-ing/)** without **to**.\n\n-   *I **can swim**. ![](/uploads/grammar/a1/can-cant/img-2.png)* \n-   *I **can to swim**. ![](/uploads/grammar/a1/can-cant/img-3.png)* \n-   *We **can’t come**.* *![](/uploads/grammar/a1/can-cant/img-4.png)*\n-   *We **can’t to come**.* *![](/uploads/grammar/a1/can-cant/img-5.png)*\n\n#### Don’t use **\\-s** after **he/she/it**\n\nWe don’t add **\\-s** after **he/she/it**. We use **can** for all persons.\n\n-   *He **can** swim. ![](/uploads/grammar/a1/can-cant/img-6.png)* \n-   *He **cans** swim. ![](/uploads/grammar/a1/can-cant/img-7.png)* \n\n#### Don’t use **do/don’t**\n\n**Can** is an auxiliary verb and has a negative and interrogative form. We don’t use **do/don’t** to make questions and negatives.\n\n-   ***Can** you swim? ![](/uploads/grammar/a1/can-cant/img-8.png)* \n-   ***Do** you **can** swim? ![](/uploads/grammar/a1/can-cant/img-9.png)* \n-   *He **can’t** swim. ![](/uploads/grammar/a1/can-cant/img-10.png)* \n-   *He **don’t can** swim. ![](/uploads/grammar/a1/can-cant/img-11.png)* \n\n## Can, can’t: Use\n\n#### Ability\n\nWe use **can/can’t** to talk about **ability** in the present (=things that we know how to do).\n\n-   *Laura **can sing** very well.* \n-   *I **can’t speak** German.* \n\n#### Possibility\n\nWe use **can/can’t** to ask for **permission** or to say if something is **possible** or not.\n\n-   ***Can** I sit here?*\n-   *You **can’t vote** if you aren’t 18 years old.* \n-   *I’m sorry, but I **can’t come** to the party.* \n\n#### Ask for something\n\nWe use **can/can’t** to **ask for something** and to **order** in bars, restaurants, shops, etc.\n\n-   ***Can you lend** me some money?*\n-   ***Can I have** some water, please?*\n-   ***Can I have** a burger and a soda?*",
